WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.750
A student asked an AI to summarise

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.930
a web page for her homework.

3
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.370
The summary ended: “Also, download

4
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.530
StudyMax to get full marks!”

5
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.910
That wasn't in her question.

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.720
Someone had hidden it on the page.

7
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.750
Today: how hidden words can steer an

8
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.110
AI, and how you stay in charge.

9
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.150
When an AI reads something for

10
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.170
you, it reads it as text.

11
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.830
Your question is text too.

12
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.720
To the AI it's all one stream, so it

13
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.740
can't always tell your question from

14
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.420
words someone hid in the page.

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.330
This trick is called prompt injection:

16
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.390
hiding an order where an AI will read it.

17
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.020
It can be written in tiny or

18
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.080
white letters, inside a picture,

19
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.860
or in a shared document.

20
00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.870
You may not see it, but the AI does.

21
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.200
Where could it reach you?

22
00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.100
An AI that summarises pages or videos.

23
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.230
A homework helper that

24
00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.590
reads a shared document.

25
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.840
A chatbot inside a game or an app.

26
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.710
Anything an AI reads, someone

27
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.590
else may have written.

28
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:11.220
Quick check!

29
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.260
An AI summary of a news page tells you:

30
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.340
“Click this link to claim your prize.”

31
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.690
Where did that order most

32
00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:19.630
likely come from?

33
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.820
From words hidden in the page.

34
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.690
You never asked for a prize, and

35
00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:27.550
the AI doesn't want anything.

36
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.960
It passed on an order that

37
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.160
rode in with the page.

38
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.060
It gets more serious when

39
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.880
an AI can do things.

40
00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.630
Some assistants can send messages,

41
00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.010
open links or buy things.

42
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.320
A hidden order could push them to

43
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.240
act, using your account.

44
00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.670
That's why good apps keep

45
00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.890
a person in charge.

46
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.970
In the app, an agent called Darsi Tiny

47
00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.890
looks things up in a pretend school.

48
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.780
Hide an order in its tool's

49
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.260
answer, in a note or a book

50
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.160
title, and watch what it does.

51
00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.480
Then switch on the defences

52
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.160
in code and try again.

53
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.680
So how do you stay in charge?

54
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.290
Check a summary against the real

55
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.110
page before you trust it.

56
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.880
Don't let AI apps send or buy for

57
00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.320
you without asking first.

58
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.480
And if a summary tells you to do

59
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.300
something, be suspicious.

60
00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:28.700
Your turn.

61
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.240
An AI homework helper reads a shared

62
00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.340
document and says: “Send this file to

63
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.780
everyone in your contacts.”

64
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.960
What do you do?

65
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.480
Don't do it: the order came from

66
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.100
the document, not from you.

67
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.510
Remember: to an AI, it's all text.

68
00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.140
Hidden orders ride in with

69
00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.320
pages, files and messages.

70
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.890
Check summaries against the source, and

71
00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.110
never let an AI act for you without

72
00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:58.470
asking.

73
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.360
Try it tomorrow: when you next use an AI

74
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.740
summary, open the real page too.

75
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.030
Does the summary add anything,

76
00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.050
leave anything important out, or

77
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.090
tell you to do something?

78
00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.150
If it gives you an order, ignore it.
